# .dockerignore — keep the build context lean (mirrors the fks repo pattern).
# The spot-portfolio image builds with context = THIS REPO ROOT, so target/
# dirs and VCS metadata must stay out of the context.

# Version control / CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Rust build artifacts
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
**/*.rmeta
*.pdb
.sqlx/

# Docs (keep READMEs out of images; nothing COPYs them)
*.md

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
.claude

# Logs / data
*.log
*.jsonl
logs/

# Archives
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# Timestamped backups of the live-money config. The Dockerfile stages configs
# with the glob `spot-portfolio*.toml*` — the trailing `*` means a
# `spot-portfolio.toml.bak.<stamp>` MATCHES and would be copied into the build.
# It is never the file the bot loads, so it can only ship a stale copy of live
# allocations into an image. Keep it out of the context entirely.
bots/spot-portfolio/spot-portfolio.toml.bak.*
